## 4. Functional Requirements

* **FR-1 (Background Upload):** The system must allow users to upload a single background scene image via drag-and-drop or file picker. Supported formats: `JPG`, `PNG`, `WEBP`; maximum raw file size: `10MB`. Must render an instant preview with "Replace" and "Remove" controls.
* **FR-2 (Object Input — Dual Mode):** The system must allow users to provide **any** target object via two mutually exclusive modes:
1. **Custom Upload:** Upload any object photo (`JPG`, `PNG`, `WEBP`, max `10MB`) with instant preview and "Replace/Remove" controls.
2. **Sample Catalog:** Select from 8–10 pre-loaded sample objects spanning multiple categories (furniture, lighting, plants, wall art, tabletop/appliances) stored as static optimized assets.


* **FR-3 (Variation Count Slider):** The system must provide a numeric range slider allowing the user to select between `1` and `3` variations (step `1`), with the default value set to `2`.
* **FR-4 (Optional Placement Instructions):** The system must provide an optional text field (max `300` characters) where users can specify placement, orientation, or styling preferences (e.g., `"Place on the wooden table near the window"`). When left empty, the system must automatically determine the most natural position, orientation, and scale.
* **FR-5 (Physics & Realism Directive):** Every AI generation request must enforce realistic physical integration: matching room perspective and horizon line, proportional real-world scale, consistent ambient and directional lighting, grounded contact/cast shadows, natural reflections/occlusion, and preservation of unaltered room regions.
* **FR-6 (AI Generation Trigger):** The "Generate Variations" button must remain disabled until both a valid background image and a valid object input are present. Clicking it submits both images, the variation count, and optional instructions to the serverless backend.
* **FR-7 (Parallel Variation Generation):** When generating multiple variations (2 or 3), the backend must execute AI generation requests concurrently with distinct subtle compositional variation cues (e.g., slight angle, positioning, or styling nuance) so each returned image is meaningfully distinct while keeping total response time under 30 seconds.
* **FR-8 (Asynchronous UI & Duplicate Lock):** While a generation request is in flight, the UI must display skeleton placeholders matching the selected variation count, show clear progress status text, and disable all form inputs and submit buttons to prevent duplicate submissions.
* **FR-9 (Results Gallery & Full-Screen Viewer):** The system must render generated variations in a clean grid (desktop) or swipeable/stacked gallery (mobile). Clicking any variation must open a full-screen lightbox supporting keyboard/arrow navigation and before/after comparison against the uploaded background.
* **FR-10 (Download & Regenerate):** Users must be able to download any individual generated image in high resolution (`PNG` or `JPG`) and click "Regenerate" to generate a fresh batch using the same (or newly edited) inputs without re-uploading images.
* **FR-11 (Image Optimization):** Oversized uploads must be resized (max `2048px` longest edge) and compressed on the client before transmission, with server-side validation as a safety net.
* **FR-12 (Temporary Storage & Auto-Cleanup):** Uploaded and generated images stored on the backend must automatically expire and delete after `24 hours` via storage lifecycle rules.
* **FR-13 (Unrestricted Demo Access):** No user authentication, account creation, payment checks, or IP rate limiting shall block requests in the MVP demo build.
* **FR-14 (Graceful Error Handling):** The system must catch and present human-readable error messages with retry options for invalid formats, oversized files, timeouts, network errors, AI safety refusals, and partial generation failures.

