## 6. Design Considerations

### Layout & Visual Flow (Single-Page 3-Step Workspace)

Use a clean, distraction-free single-page layout so users see the entire workflow immediately:

1. **Header Bar:** App title ("AI Room & Object Visualizer"), brief 1-line subtitle, and a "Start Over" button (visible once inputs or results exist).
2. **Input Workspace (2-column split on desktop, vertical stack on mobile):**
* **Step 1 Card — Upload Scene:** Large dashed dropzone (`min-h-[260px]`) showing accepted formats (`JPG, PNG, WEBP • Max 10MB`). Once uploaded, switches to a crisp full-bleed `object-contain` preview with floating "Replace" and "Remove" action pills.
* **Step 2 Card — Choose Object:** Segmented tab toggle (`Upload Any Object` | `Sample Catalog`).
* *Upload tab:* Identical dropzone UX to Step 1.
* *Catalog tab:* Scrollable 2x4 (mobile) / 3x3 (desktop) grid of 8–10 diverse sample items on clean neutral backgrounds with labels.




3. **Controls Bar (Step 3 — Configure & Generate):**
* **Variation Slider:** Labeled `Variations (1–3)` with snap ticks `1`, `2`, `3` and default handle at `2`.
* **Optional Instructions Input:** Single-line or expandable 2-row textarea with `0/300` counter and subtle helper text: *"Optional: Leave blank for automatic realistic placement."*
* **Primary CTA:** High-contrast `"Generate 2 Variations"` button (dynamically reflects the slider count; disabled with clear muted styling until Steps 1 and 2 are complete).


4. **Results Section (appears below workspace and auto-scrolls smoothly into view on generation):**
* Loading state: Pulsing skeleton cards matching the selected count + progress status banner.
* Success state: Responsive grid (2 columns for 2 outputs, 3 columns on wide desktop for 3 outputs; swipeable carousel/stack on mobile) with top-right **"Regenerate"** button.
* Each card has hover/always-visible mobile actions: **Expand (Full Screen)** and **Download**.


5. **Full-Screen Lightbox Modal:**
* Dark translucent backdrop (`bg-black/90`), centered high-res image, left/right arrows, close (`X`) button, **"Hold to Compare Original"** button (toggles back to the raw background photo while pressed), and **"Download HD"** button.



