## 7. Technical Considerations (Complete End-to-End Implementation Blueprint)

### 7.1 Recommended Serverless Architecture & Tech Stack

This architecture avoids always-on VMs and Docker containers, deploys directly from Git, and handles parallel image inference cleanly:

| Layer | Technology Choice | Rationale |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **Frontend Framework** | **React 19 + TypeScript + Vite** | Fast dev loop, strict type safety, zero unnecessary SSR complexity for a stateless interactive tool. |
| **Styling & UI Primitives** | **Tailwind CSS v4 + Lucide Icons + Radix UI (Dialog/Slider)** | Accessible slider and full-screen lightbox out of the box; responsive utility layout. |
| **Client Image Processing** | **`browser-image-compression` (or HTML5 Canvas + `createImageBitmap`)** | Resizes photos to max `2048px`, fixes mobile EXIF rotation, cuts upload payload by 70–85%. |
| **Hosting & Serverless API** | **Cloudflare Workers (with Static Assets / Pages)** *or* **Vercel Serverless Functions** | Zero idle cost, global edge delivery, direct bindings to object storage. Set function timeout to **60 seconds** (safety buffer over the 30s target). |
| **Temporary Object Storage** | **Cloudflare R2** (zero egress fees) [cite: 1.3.3] | Native 1-day object lifecycle expiration removes temporary files automatically within 24 hours. |
| **Primary AI Image Model** | **Google Gemini API — `gemini-nano-banana-2.1**` (`@google/genai` SDK) | Supports multi-image reference composition (up to 14 reference images, up to 6 high-fidelity object images), built-in Thinking mode for spatial/compositional logic, 1K/2K/4K output, and Flash-level speed. |
| **Fallback AI Image Model** | **OpenAI Images API — `gpt-image-2.6-sunburst**` (or `gpt-image-2.6-flare`) | Active 2026 replacement for the retired `gpt-image-1` model; supports multi-image editing and high-fidelity composition. |

