### 7.9 Error Handling Matrix

| Failure Scenario | HTTP Code / Trigger | User-Facing Message | Recovery Behavior |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Unsupported file format (e.g., GIF, HEIC, PDF) | Client check / `400 INVALID_FILE_TYPE` | `"Please upload a JPG, PNG, or WEBP image."` | Rejects file cleanly; preserves existing valid input in other step. |
| Oversized file (over 10MB) | Client check / `413 FILE_TOO_LARGE` | `"Image must be 10MB or smaller. Please choose a smaller photo."` | Rejects file cleanly; no upload sent. |
| AI safety filter refusal | `422 CONTENT_BLOCKED` | `"The AI couldn't process one of these images due to safety guidelines. Try a different photo or rephrase your instructions."` | Re-enables controls; keeps inputs visible for quick swap. |
| Partial variation failure (e.g., 1 of 2 fails) | `200 OK` with `warnings[]` | `"Generated 1 of 2 variations. Click Regenerate to try again."` | Displays successful image(s) with non-blocking warning banner. |
| Request timeout (over 45 seconds) | Client `AbortController` / `504 TIMEOUT` | `"Generation took longer than expected. Please try again."` | Cancels loading state; "Try Again" button retries immediately. |
| Network / AI provider outage | `502 UPSTREAM_ERROR` / Fetch error | `"Couldn't reach the image generator right now. Please try again in a moment."` | Re-enables controls; inputs remain intact. |
| Expired download link (after 24 hours) | `404 NOT_FOUND` | `"This temporary image has expired (images are deleted after 24 hours). Click Regenerate to create new ones."` | Prompts user to regenerate. |

